        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Persist Claw artifact provenance refs",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Reuses this draft PR as mutating apply PR1 for Claws, stacked on #101328 and aligned with RFC PR openclaw/rfcs#27.\n- Adds Claw-owned SQLite provenance tables for apply records and package-like artifact references.\n- Adds an explicit `--yes` gate for `claws apply` and `claws feed apply`; `--dry-run` keeps returning the non-mutating plan.\n- Persists supported skill/plugin/MCP artifact references and shared ref accounting. Workspace/persona/automation entries remain preview-only in this slice.\n\nThis does not run real skill/plugin/MCP installers yet. The persisted result intentionally reports `recordedArtifactRefs` and ownership state `referenced`/`shared`, leaving actual install ownership for the next mutating apply PR.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: openclaw/rfcs#27\n- Depends on: #101328\n- This PR: first mutating apply slice, artifact provenance/ref accounting\n- Follow-up: wire real artifact installers and remove semantics using the persisted ref accounting\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/claws/schema.test.ts src/claws/provenance.test.ts src/cli/claws-cli.test.ts src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts src/cli/program/command-registry.test.ts src/cli/program/root-command-descriptions.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check && node scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.mjs`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed:\n`claws apply` can now move past dry-run only mode when the caller explicitly passes `--yes`, recording Claw package-like artifact provenance/ref accounting in shared OpenClaw state while keeping workspace and automation entries preview-only.\n\nReal environment tested:\nWSL Ubuntu 24.04 worktree `/root/src/openclaw-claws-pr3`, source CLI harness via `node --import tsx`, isolated `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=/tmp/openclaw-claws-mutating-pr1-proof-state`, bundled plugins disabled with `OPENCLAW_DISABLE_BUNDLED_PLUGINS=1`.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n1. `rm -rf /tmp/openclaw-claws-mutating-pr1-proof-state`\n2. `OPENCLAW_DISABLE_BUNDLED_PLUGINS=1 OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=/tmp/openclaw-claws-mutating-pr1-proof-state node --import tsx src/entry.ts claws apply src/claws/fixtures/incident-response.claw.json --yes --json > /tmp/claws-apply-result.json`\n3. Queried `/tmp/openclaw-claws-mutating-pr1-proof-state/state/openclaw.sqlite` for `claw_artifact_refs`.\n\nEvidence after fix:\nJSON result summary:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"openclaw.clawApplyResult.v1\",\n  \"dryRun\": false,\n  \"mutationAllowed\": true,\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"totalEntries\": 5,\n    \"recordedArtifactRefs\": 3,\n    \"previewOnlyEntries\": 2,\n    \"skippedUnsupported\": 0,\n    \"blockedEntries\": 0,\n    \"provenanceRecords\": 3\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSQLite rows recorded:\n\n```text\nincident-triage-skill  skills:clawhub:incident-triage@1.0.0\npager-duty-plugin      plugins:npm:@openclaw/plugin-pager-duty@2.4.0\nstatuspage-mcp         mcpServers:clawhub:statuspage-mcp@1.1.0\n```\n\nObserved result after fix:\nThe apply command succeeded only with `--yes`, emitted `openclaw.clawApplyResult.v1`, recorded three package-like artifact refs in shared SQLite state, and reported two preview-only entries for non-artifact lifecycle work.\n\nWhat was not tested:\nReal artifact installer execution and remove/uninstall semantics are not implemented in this PR; they are follow-up mutating apply slices.\n",
